Design a premium, modern, fully responsive, and interactive Course Page for "YourLearner" — a learning platform for programming education. Create a high-fidelity UI/UX prototype only (no backend implementation required).

Design Goals:

Clean, modern, engaging, and distraction-free learning experience
Similar quality to Codecademy, Scrimba, DataCamp, freeCodeCamp, Coursera, and Duolingo
Unique identity for YourLearner with its own branding
Beautiful spacing, rounded cards, smooth animations, meaningful icons, and intuitive layout
Pages & Sections to Design:

1. Course Landing Page

Large page title and motivational subtitle
Overall learning progress and current streak display
Search bar and filter options
"Continue Learning" button
Two large learning path cards (Beginner & Intermediate) showing:
Path icon, description, total topics, estimated duration, difficulty, progress, and continue button
2. Topic List View

Complete list of topics for selected learning path
Each topic card shows: icon, title, description, estimated time, difficulty, completion status, lock/unlock status, progress, and continue button
Locked topics appear disabled until previous assessment is passed
3. Learning Page (Split Interface)

Left Side: Lesson content including:
Topic title, introduction, learning objectives, key concepts, detailed explanation, step-by-step examples, Python syntax, visual diagrams, flowcharts, best practices, common mistakes, tips, real-world examples, summary
Previous/Next topic navigation
Right Side: Sticky Python Compiler with:
Code editor with syntax highlighting, run button, reset button, copy code, output console
4. Notes Section

Read/write/edit/save personal notes
Future: download notes, export PDF
5. Quiz Section

Multiple choice questions with one correct answer
Instant feedback, correct answer explanation, quiz score, progress indicator
6. Topic Assessment

7 questions total, minimum 6 correct to pass
Pass: unlock next topic | Fail: keep locked
Show: "You need at least 6 correct answers to unlock the next lesson."
Options: Review Lesson, Retry Assessment
7. Resources Section

Official documentation, helpful articles, video tutorials, practice websites, cheat sheets, downloadable PDFs, GitHub repository
8. Course Progress Dashboard

Overall progress, completed/remaining topics, current topic, quiz scores, assessment status, completion percentage
9. Sidebar (Sticky)

Course overview, topic list, notes, quiz, assessment, resources, progress
Current topic highlighted
10. Header

Topic title, breadcrumb navigation, search, profile, notifications, current progress
11. Footer

Previous topic, next topic, mark as completed, back to course
UI Style Requirements:

Modern cards, rounded corners, soft shadows, premium typography, blue gradient accents, meaningful icons, smooth hover effects, page transitions, micro-interactions, loading animations, responsive design, dark/light mode ready, sticky navigation, beautiful empty states, modern progress bars, animated circular progress, clean layout, excellent spacing, minimal design
User Experience Goals:

Premium and interactive feel
Never overwhelming
Distraction-free reading
Compiler always accessible while studying
Smooth navigation between topics
Clear understanding of completed vs. remaining work
Important:

Build only the complete UI/UX prototype
Use realistic placeholder data
Every button, card, modal, tab, and interaction should appear fully functional
Maintain consistent design system across entire Course module
Ensure design is scalable for adding more programming languages
Final result should feel like a polished, production-ready learning platform
